            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nThis is a deliberate design choice, I'd imagine majority of 'mini.icons' users will see file named 'init.lua' only when dealing with Neovim config or plugins.\r\n\r\nYou can disable it with the following config:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire('mini.icons').setup({\r\n  file = {\r\n    ['init.lua'] = { glyph = '󰢱', hl = 'MiniIconsAzure' },\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nClosing as working as intended.",
