            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I'd imagine majority of 'mini.icons' users will see file named 'init.lua' only when dealing with Neovim\r\n\r\nThat may be true, but for the rest of us, the plugin will by default show a completely wrong icon.\r\n\r\nWouldn't it simply be possible to add an extra condition, e.g., requiring that the path of the `init.lua` must have the string `nvim` somewhere?",
