        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Wouldn't it simply be possible to add an extra condition, e.g., requiring that the path of the `init.lua` must have the string `nvim` somewhere?\r\n\r\nNope, for several reasons:\r\n- Customizing icons for `'file'` category can be done only based on file name. Including default values. Any more than that would require setting custom filetype for files which are named 'init.lua' and are descendants of 'nvim' directory.\r\n- For it to be more useful, users/plugins should supply full path to `MiniIcons.get('file', path)`. This is currently not the case in general (aside 'mini.nvim' modules) due to most plugins using 'nvim-web-devicons' interface only uses file basenames.\r\n\r\n> That may be true, but for the rest of us, the plugin will by default show a completely wrong icon.\r\n\r\nMy hope is that either adjusting custom config or not caring much about this little Easter egg would not be a big burden.",
